The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (sechdrs[i].sh_flags & SHF_EXECINSTR &&
    pi->ehdr->e_entry >= sechdrs[i].sh_addr &&
    pi->ehdr->e_entry < (sechdrs[i].sh_addr + sechdrs[i].sh_size) &&
    !WARN_ON(kbuf->image->start != pi->ehdr->e_entry)) {
    kbuf->image->start -= sechdrs[i].sh_addr;
    kbuf->image->start += kbuf->mem + offset;
}
```
Reason:  
When multiple executable sections have overlapping `sh_addr`, the same `e_entry` falls within the address range of each such section. The original code iterates over all sections and applies the adjustment for every match. After the first match, `image->start` is changed from `e_entry` to a new address, so the second match triggers the `WARN_ON` because `kbuf->image->start != pi->ehdr->e_entry`. This results in an unwanted warning and a potentially incorrect entry point.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
entry_sym = kexec_purgatory_find_symbol(pi, "purgatory_start");
if (entry_sym) {
    entry_shndx = entry_sym->st_shndx;
    entry_off = entry_sym->st_value;
}
...
if (!start_fixed && entry_sym && i == entry_shndx &&
    (sechdrs[i].sh_flags & SHF_EXECINSTR) &&
    entry_off < sechdrs[i].sh_size) {
    kbuf->image->start = kbuf->mem + offset + entry_off;
    start_fixed = true;
}
...
if (!start_fixed && sechdrs[i].sh_flags & SHF_EXECINSTR &&
    pi->ehdr->e_entry >= sechdrs[i].sh_addr &&
    pi->ehdr->e_entry < (sechdrs[i].sh_addr + sechdrs[i].sh_size) &&
    kbuf->image->start == pi->ehdr->e_entry) {
    kbuf->image->start -= sechdrs[i].sh_addr;
    kbuf->image->start += kbuf->mem + offset;
    start_fixed = true;
}
```
Reason:  
The fix introduces two improvements:  
1. If a `purgatory_start` symbol exists, its section and offset are used to compute `image->start` exactly once, bypassing the ambiguous `e_entry` matching.  
2. The original `e_entry`-based fallback is guarded by `!start_fixed` to prevent multiple matches. The `WARN_ON` is removed because after the first adjustment `start_fixed` becomes `true`, so subsequent sections will skip the block entirely. This ensures the entry point is set only once, avoiding the warning and maintaining correctness.

criterion:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (sechdrs[i].sh_flags & SHF_EXECINSTR &&
    pi->ehdr->e_entry >= sechdrs[i].sh_addr &&
    pi->ehdr->e_entry < (sechdrs[i].sh_addr + sechdrs[i].sh_size) &&
